Part 6: restricted adversary (zeta-like constraints), NUMERICAL
  scaling (memo sec.1): zeta zero 1/2 + i gamma + (beta - 1/2) -> z = gamma - i(beta-1/2), multiplied by L = log T/(2 pi):
  mean spacing 1 (density 1), scaled height v = (beta - 1/2) log T/(2 pi).  Selberg N(sigma,T) << T^{1-(sigma-1/2)/4} log T
  gives #{v' >= v} << N e^{-pi v/2}: no constraint at the relevant heights v <= 0.5.
  density exactly 1 (M = N), no cap                                       : 120 patterns, min ratio 1.000861 (max v 0.0e+00)
  density exactly 1 (M = N), off-line <= 7/12 (PRZZ: >= 5/12 on the line) : 120 patterns, min ratio 1.000861 (max v 0.0e+00)
